From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:30:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix and harden the public lobby announce

A public room registers with the lobby web service, updates it every 15
seconds and unregisters when it stops. Since upstream moved to Jacinth
and Hydrocarbon (83fde0738) and to std::format (d3ee883e5), a public
room drops out of the lobby the first time anyone joins and never comes
back:

- Players were serialised by Jacinth's reflection: every Member field,
  with the game as a nested object. The lobby answers every update that
  lists a player with 422 Unprocessable Entity, and drops the room after
  a few minutes without a valid update. The lobby's own format is
  restored (as nlohmann's to_json/from_json wrote it): username and
  avatarUrl only when set, nickname, and a flat gameName and gameId.
- Error results carried hydro::Status as it formats, "404 Not Found".
  The announce loop re-registers a dropped room only when the result is
  "404", and the web client retries with a new JWT only on "401", so
  neither happened: the room logged a 404 every 15 seconds and stayed
  unlisted. Results now carry the bare status code; the log line keeps
  the reason phrase.

Hardening:

- Every lobby request went out as POST since the move to Hydrocarbon,
  whatever the caller asked for: the room fetched the JWT public key
  with a POST and "unregistered" with a POST to /lobby/<id>, so it
  stayed listed after stopping. Requests now use their own method
  (hydro::perform).
- RoomJson::Register read the lobby's reply without checking it. An
  empty, non-JSON or incomplete reply (a proxy error page, an outage)
  registered the room with an empty id. Empty replies, parse errors and
  a missing "id" now return a WrongContent WebResult, which the session
  reports like any other announce error.
- The announce thread is wrapped in a try/catch, so an exception is
  logged instead of calling std::terminate. The thread still ends: the
  room keeps running, unannounced.
- RoomJson::Delete unregistered the room on a thread that used the
  RoomJson's own client and room_id, kept in a jthread member that was
  destroyed after them, and the room crashed on the way out (a segfault
  in memmove; upstream since c2e74a938, July 2026). The web client also
  has no read timeout, so a slow lobby could hold the room past docker
  stop's 10 seconds. The DELETE now runs on its own thread with copies of
  what it needs (3 seconds to connect), and the destructor waits for it
  up to 5 seconds; the room unregisters if the lobby answers in time and
  stops either way.
- Every player without a lobby token logged "Verification failed" at
  Info level. Only that exact case (cpp-jwt's "decode"/2,
  SignatureFormatError, from an empty token) is silenced; expired tokens
  and bad signatures are still logged.

Tests: tests/test_room_protocol.py runs a public room against a stand-in
lobby that checks the format of every update and of the players in it,
answers one update with 404 and requires the room to register again,
and stops the room while the lobby is still answering the DELETE: it
requires a clean exit and a DELETE request, also within 10 seconds when
the lobby takes 25 seconds to answer. It also checks that joining
without a token still works. JWT verification against the real lobby is
not covered.
